<concept id="t00110">
	<title>Sunroof open warning</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>panorama sunroof
					<indexterm>sunroof open warning</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e00564">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e00565">
								<image href="images/N_SP3i25_C00_002_IR.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>If the sunroof is not fully closed when the driver turns off the engine, a warning chime sounds for several seconds, and a warning appears on the instrument cluster display.</p>
		<p>Close the sunroof securely when leaving your vehicle.</p>
		<note type="note">
			<p>Make sure the sunroof is closed fully when leaving your vehicle. If you leave the sunroof open, it may invite theft, and rain or snow may wet the interior.</p>
		</note>
	</conbody>
